            <ArticleTitle>Kawasaki disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kawasaki disease is an acute vasculitis of small- and medium-sized blood vessels which was first described by Dr Tomisaku Kawasaki in 1967. Involvement of the coronary arteries is common and may be life threatening or cause long-term cardiovascular complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
